SecureDMARC is a high-performance DMARC policy evaluation milter (RFC 7489)
written in Zig with a thread-per-core architecture using kqueue.

It reads upstream SPF and DKIM Authentication-Results headers, fetches the
sender domain's _dmarc. TXT record, evaluates identifier alignment (strict
or relaxed mode), and adds its own Authentication-Results header with the
DMARC verdict (pass/fail/none/temperror/permerror).

Must run after SecureSPF and SecureDKIM in the Postfix milter chain.
